# Everything here is excluded from the Docker build context — the set of files
# sent to the Docker daemon before the build starts.
#
# This matters for two reasons:
#   1. Speed. node_modules is hundreds of megabytes; shipping it to the daemon
#      on every build is slow, and the image rebuilds it anyway.
#   2. SECURITY. Anything copied into an image can be extracted from that image
#      by anyone who can pull it. `.env` holds your production database password
#      and JWT secret and must never be baked in — secrets are supplied at RUN
#      time by docker-compose, never at BUILD time.

node_modules
dist
coverage
.git
.gitignore

# Secrets — never in an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated Prisma Client: regenerated inside the build from schema.prisma, and
# the host copy may have been built for a different platform.
src/generated

# Local tooling and docs, irrelevant to the runtime
.vscode
.idea
.agents
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Test artefacts
test
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
